# ── INTRODUCTION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
add_heading(doc, '1. Introduction', level=1)
add_body(doc, 'This Workforce Management Document provides a comprehensive reference for the execution of Distribution EPC (Engineering, Procurement, and Construction) projects undertaken by the organization on behalf of Distribution Companies (DISCOMs) and government utilities across India. The document captures the structured workflows, process sequences, and technical activities that govern each phase of a Distribution EPC project from initial bid preparation through final contract closure.')
add_body(doc, 'Distribution EPC projects encompass the design, supply, and construction of high tension (HT) overhead lines, low tension (LT) distribution networks, distribution transformer (DTR) installations, underground cable systems, smart metering and Advanced Metering Infrastructure (AMI), distribution automation and SCADA systems, and associated civil and electrical infrastructure under schemes including RDSS (Revamped Distribution Sector Scheme), DDUGJY (Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Gram Jyoti Yojana), SAUBHAGYA, and Smart Cities Mission.')
add_body(doc, 'Each workflow section documents the logical sequence of activities, parallel execution opportunities, sequential dependency gates, and system status transitions that apply to that phase of the project. The document is intended as a reference for Project Managers, Site Engineers, QA/QC personnel, procurement teams, and contract managers engaged in Distribution EPC project execution.')

